2026-10-23T05:39:48.5284697Z    image gate: coleman_ames_house_1811_prairie inland_architect_plate: verdict "differs", 4 difference(s) open: the bay's south-return downpipe: the plate's pale rod at x 298-302 px, from a head under the bay's cornice, runs down the return's own south face about 0.3 m in from the front's corner (a 1.0 m return at v 5.99 hides the main wall from x 288 to 315 px, so it cannot stand on the main front there); K01's front pipes run only along the street front, so T-2993 stands it on the main front beside the return at 6.24 m, landing at x 320-326 px, about 21 px south of the plate's (T-2997); the porch's south return: beside the arch, from about x 467 to 507 px, the plate opens the entrance block's south return as a small arcade of round-arched lights on colonnettes with carved capitals, lighting the porch from the side; the build closes it in coursed stone (T-2991); the arcade's capitals (y 680-690 px) and crowns (y 647-660) step down across x 476-501, so it stands on a face receding from the front, about v 9.4-9.5 by the camera, short of the solved south corner at v 10.40; T-3005's re-read: the corner is ROUNDED, about 0.9 m radius, its front tangent at x 467-470 (v about 9.5) and its far side at about x 515-520 (the solve's x 510 is that edge), the downpipe's shoe at about y 816 px on the south face just behind it; the colonnettes step down because they run round the curve (on a 0.9 m radius, x 476, 490 and 501 px stand at about 8, 27 and 44 degrees from the front), not along a flat return. K01 has no rounded corner (T-3006); the arcade then stands on it (T-2991); T-3006 has built the round (0.9 m from grade, coursed on the front's beds), so the arcade now has its curve to stand on (T-2991, after the oriel's T-3007); the bay's stone gable's centre: its apex, its lights and its pinnacles stand about 10 px (0.25 m) south of the plate's (the apex at x about 209 px against 196, the flat-headed lights' centre at 208 against 197), as T-2542 placed the gable on the bay's centre; and the plate's pinnacles are carved, the right-hand one capped by a scaled dome, the left by a moulded block, where the build's are square shafts under pyramids (T-3051); the south gable's rear fall: behind the tall stack the plate's coping runs from about (528, 380) to (557, 453) px, about 30 px under the render's (522, 322) to (555, 417), parallel to it, so the rear fall stands lower than the coped rake built at the ridge + 0.3 m falling to the rear wall head; the second stack stands on that lower line in the plate. Read the flank's wall head and the rear slope against the Chicagology print (T-3051)
