2026-10-23T05:53:59.1963587Z comment 1616 "{\n  \"body\": \"PR stuck: the gate is red and the run that owned it has finished (`aaaaaaaa`).\\n\\nThe `gate` check run on this head completed **failure**, and the steward run that\\nowns this branch has finished. Nothing in this repository is coming back for it:\\n\\n* `.github/steward/pr-lap.sh` merges `dev` in and pushes. It does NOT gate — that\\n  cost ~7 minutes a PR and was why the queue never converged — so a red gate is\\n  not something it can notice, let alone fix.\\n* `.github/steward/merge-ready.sh` merges only what GitHub calls `clean`, and a PR\\n  with a failing required check is never `clean`.\\n* The run that would have pushed a fix is over. On 2026-09-21 two runs finished\\n  SUCCESS while leaving a red PR behind (#1616, #1618), which is what this\\n  report exists to stop being silent about.\\n\\nThe step(s) that failed:\\n\\n  * Does this change carry a changelog entry?\\n\\n`./tools/preflight.sh` asks that question BEFORE the PR is opened, against the\\nmerge base and with the same shas the workflow uses. It is out of `check.sh` on\\npurpose — the bake regenerates `data/` and correctly ships no entry — which is\\nwhy running the gate alone cannot find it. AGENTS.md has required preflight\\nbefore a PR is opened since 2026-09-10.\\n\\nThis reporter does not re-run, revert or repair anything, and that is deliberate:\\nboth of the PRs above needed real judgement (a rule that had stopped firing and\\nhad to be retired; a report whose prose contradicted its own table), and a robot\\nthat had guessed at either would have been worse than the silence.\\n\\nWhat clears it:\\n\\n1. Reproduce the failing step in a clone of this branch with `dev` merged in,\\n   fix it, and push. The gate re-runs on the push and `merge-ready` takes it.\\n2. If the failure is not this PR's — red on `dev` too — say so on the PR and\\n   port the fix rather than widening this branch.\\n3. Or close it and re-cut the work on a current `dev`.\\n\\nIf it is waiting on the OWNER on purpose, park it with `hold` — this reporter\\nreads labels first and leaves a held PR alone. If it is merely UNFINISHED, hand\\nit to the next run instead:\\n\\n    .github/steward/pr-rest.sh resume 1616 --why \\\"...\\\" --waits-on nothing\\n\\nwhich writes the reason where a machine and a person can both read it.\\n\\n---\\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\\n\"\n}\n"
